    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d904">

                <pb facs="1077" n="981" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg981"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Moore to Sir Julian Pauncefote.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1898-06-21"><hi rendition="#italic">June 21,
                        1898</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Sir Julian</hi>: I return herewith your telegram
                    to Sir Alexander Gollan and his reply, which you were so good as to leave with
                    me, and inclose a paper containing a statement of the matters on which we hope
                    to obtain information through Sir Alexander Gollan and Her Majesty’s consul at
                    Santiago de Cuba. I have put the statement into the form of a telegram to Sir
                    Alexander Gollan in case you should rind it convenient to use it for that
                    purpose.</p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">J. B. Moore.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>



                <xi:include href="d904-a1.xml" xpointer="d904-a1"/>
